

rgn_estimate_number_of_insns used the LUID span of a block and then
subtracted the debug insns in it.  Notes take the LUID of the following
insn, so when the last non-debug element of a block is a note, the
debug insns after it were subtracted once too often.  A block with only
debug insns was counted as -1 insns with -g and 0 with -g0, and
too_large could accept a region with -g only.

Count the non-debug insns directly instead.  The exact count is normally
one greater than the previous LUID-span estimate, so this also increases
the -g0 estimate by one for most blocks.

Regression tested on an aarch64-linux-gnu cross compiler (c, c++) with
binutils and glibc, running execution tests under qemu-user.  No existing
test result changed; the patched tree additionally passes the new test.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5, co-reviewed by OpenAI Codex 5.6 Sol and Yongqiang Tian.

	PR rtl-optimization/128860

gcc/ChangeLog:

	* sched-rgn.cc (rgn_estimate_number_of_insns): Count the
	non-debug insns instead of using the LUID span.

gcc/testsuite/ChangeLog:

	* gcc.dg/pr128860.c: New test.

Signed-off-by: Yongqiang Tian <yqtian668@gmail.com>
---
v2: Count non-debug insns directly, as suggested by Richard.

I also logged every call to estimate_number_of_insns while compiling the
13,579 files in gcc.dg, gcc.dg/torture, and gcc.c-torture on the
aarch64-linux-gnu cross:

                                             Calls    Blocks   Maximum
  -O2 -fschedule-insns                       14,022    14,022         1
  -O3 -funroll-loops -fschedule-insns        11,491    11,491         1
  -O2, region extension, 2 iterations        64,714    59,022         2
  -O3, region extension, 10 iterations       68,828    63,718         2

Without region extension, every block was estimated exactly once.  With
region extension enabled, some blocks were estimated twice: once in
find_rgns and once when extend_rgns assembled the extended regions.  No
block was estimated more than twice in this corpus.  The largest run
averaged about 1.08 calls per block, so a cache does not appear worthwhile
for this workload.

I also compared the -g0 assembly before and after v2 over the same corpus:

  -O2 -fschedule-insns                                      0 differences
  -O3 -funroll-loops -fschedule-insns                       1 difference
  -O2 with the test's region-extension parameters         437 differences

The single -O3 difference is gcc.c-torture/compile/pr86637-2.c.  The
test parameters deliberately put the region-size limit at the boundary
exposed by the bug.  With those parameters, -fcompare-debug fails on
pr71802.c before the change and passes after it, with no remaining failure
in the corpus.

The full aarch64-linux-gnu cross testsuite, including execution tests under
qemu-user, produced:

                 gcc PASS  gcc FAIL  g++ PASS  g++ FAIL
  base             407898       133    473659         8
  v2               407899       133    473659         8

The sorted gcc.sum and g++.sum result lines differ only by the new
gcc.dg/pr128860.c PASS.

 gcc/sched-rgn.cc                | 16 +++++-----------
 gcc/testsuite/gcc.dg/pr128860.c |  8 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 gcc/testsuite/gcc.dg/pr128860.c

diff --git a/gcc/sched-rgn.cc b/gcc/sched-rgn.cc
index 08af28bcd..246d4dbf4 100644
--- a/gcc/sched-rgn.cc
+++ b/gcc/sched-rgn.cc
@@ -547,18 +547,12 @@ find_single_block_region (bool ebbs_p)
 static int
 rgn_estimate_number_of_insns (basic_block bb)
 {
-  int count;
-
-  count = INSN_LUID (BB_END (bb)) - INSN_LUID (BB_HEAD (bb));
-
-  if (MAY_HAVE_DEBUG_INSNS)
-    {
-      rtx_insn *insn;
+  int count = 0;
+  rtx_insn *insn;
 
-      FOR_BB_INSNS (bb, insn)
-	if (DEBUG_INSN_P (insn))
-	  count--;
-    }
+  FOR_BB_INSNS (bb, insn)
+    if (NONDEBUG_INSN_P (insn))
+      count++;
 
   return count;
 }
diff --git a/gcc/testsuite/gcc.dg/pr128860.c b/gcc/testsuite/gcc.dg/pr128860.c
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..51fac7ddf
--- /dev/null
+++ b/gcc/testsuite/gcc.dg/pr128860.c
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+/* PR rtl-optimization/128860 */
+/* The region size estimate must not depend on debug insns.  A block that
+   contains only debug insns used to be counted as -1 insns with -g.  */
+/* { dg-do compile } */
+/* { dg-require-effective-target scheduling } */
+/* { dg-options "-O2 -fschedule-insns -fcompare-debug -w --param max-sched-extend-regions-iters=2 --param max-sched-region-insns=7" } */
+
+#include "torture/pr71802.c"
